  "model": "gemma4:12b",
  "created_at": "2026-07-01T21:52:12.3968127Z",
  "response": "{\"campaign_title\": \"Echoes of the Silent Gate\",\n  \"campaign_subtitle\": \"The Fracture of Zenith Reach\",\n  \"campaign_logline\": \"A broken signal from an abandoned gate hub forces a desperate pilot to navigate the shifting loyalties of three warring factions in the dying light of the Zenith sector.\",\n  \"campaign_pitch\": \"You are a freelance hauler caught between the expansionist Zenith, the isolationist Aurelia, and the military Vanguard. When you recover a corrupted data-slug from a derelict station, you discover that the jump gates aren't just failing\u2014they're being silenced by something intentional.\",\n  \"campaign_story_summary\": \"The player begins in the Zenith Reach, a cluster of systems where trade routes are collapsing due to gate instability. The primary conflict involves Zenith seeking to stabilize the local grid at any cost, Aurelia trying to preserve their sovereignty from external interference, and Vanguard attempting to maintain security against 'anomalies' in the deep space. As the player takes contracts for these three groups, they begin to notice a recurring, rhythmic pulse of data that appears on all frequencies simultaneously. This signal predates known construction but persists as a haunting constant. The mystery lies in whether this is an automated failsafe, a desperate plea from a forgotten colony, or something else entirely trying to communicate.\",\n  \"tone\": \"PG-13 frontier space opera with dry, slightly dark humor\",\n  \"opening_status_quo\": \"The player starts as a broke pilot on the fringes of Zenith Reach. Trade is sluggish, and local stations are in a state of low-level panic over 'ghost' signals and fluctuating gate frequencies.\",\n  \"visible_crisis\": \"The jump gates are flickering and becoming unreliable, causing significant trade delays and safety risks for merchant ships.\",\n  \"hidden_crisis\": \"A systematic decommissioning of the local gate network is occurring from an unknown origin point deep within the infrastructure.\",\n  \"why_now\": \"A recent surge in solar radiation has 'thinned' the barriers between signal layers, making the hidden signals audible to civilian sensors for a limited window.\",\n  \"player_role\": \"Independent pilot and scavenger. You are not a hero; you are someone who can move freely where others cannot because your signature is anonymous.\",\n  \"kaelen_public_role\": \"Broker, fixer, and contract handler.\",\n  \"kaelen_secret_angle\": \"Kaelen possesses an unusually high level of technical knowledge regarding the 'pre-collapse' gate infrastructure and seems to have a personal connection to the missing signal logs.\",\n  \"main_mystery_question\": \"Who is silencing the gates?\",\n  \"main_mystery_false_answer\": \"The gates are failing because of natural decay or solar activity.\",\n  \"main_mystery_true_answer_hint\": \"The silence is a deliberate, programmed override from an unknown entity or system.\",\n  \"long_term_reveal_direction\": \"Progress toward the realization that the 'silence' is a defensive protocol for something hidden in the deep gate-space between hubs.\",\n  \"act_1_name\": \"The Static of Zenith\",\n  \"act_1_goal\": \"Identify the source of the local signal interference and secure enough resources to move beyond the first jump gate.\",\n  \"act_1_opening_incident\": \"A cargo ship from Aurelia is found drifting near a mining outpost. It contains a high-value, corrupted data-slug that Kaelen offers a bounty for its recovery.\",\n  \"act_1_midpoint_turn\": \"The player finds three different versions of the same log entry in three separate salvage sites, each belonging to a different faction's archive.\",\n  \"act_1_finale\": \"The player must choose which faction's data-port they will prioritize for their next jump, effectively choosing whose technology they are using to bypass the first gate lock.\",\n  \"act_1_player_takeaway\": \"The world is larger than the sum of its parts; every faction has a secret they are hiding from the others regarding the gate status.\",\n  \"starter_mission_title\": \"Scavenge the Drift\",\n  \"starter_mission_reason\": \"A Reaver drone, malfunctioning and desperate, attempts to intercept the player's path toward the drifting ship. It is an automated security drone that doesn't know who you are or what it's trying to protect.\",\n  \"starter_enemy_identity\": \"Reaver-class scavenger drone (malfunctioning).\",\n  \"starter_enemy_knows\": \"A fragment of a log entry: 'The gate is not open. It is closed by hand.'\",\n  \"starter_mission_aftershock\": \"Finding the data-slug causes local radar to flare, drawing attention from both Zenith and Aurelia scouts.\",\n  \"zenith_current_problem\": \"They need more raw ore to fuel their expansion plans and are losing patience with the 'gap' in their supply lines.\",\n  \"aurelia_current_problem\": \"They want to isolate themselves from the larger trade network to protect their own research projects from being leaked.\",\n  \"vanguard_current_problem\": \"They are struggling to maintain order in a sector where the other two factions are trying to outmange each other's resources.\",\n  \"faction_conflict_triangle\": \"Zenith wants more space; Aurelia wants more privacy; Vanguard is tasked with containing the mess they both create. The tension is highest when Zenith and Aurelia directly compete for the same resource nodes.\",\n  \"neutral_space_pressure\": \"The lack of reliable jumps makes the trade routes dangerous, making 'independent' pilots like the player a vital but risky commodity.\",\n  \"recurring_clue_name\": \"The Ghost Pulse\",\n  \"recurring_clue_signal\": \"A rhythmic 3-second pulse of static that appears on all channels whenever the player is getting close to a gate hub or derelict ship.\",\n  \"recurring_clue_first_ parl\u00e9\": \"A crackling, distorted audio log from a miner who mentions 'the sound' before the signal cuts out.\",\n  \"recurring_clue_escalation\": \"The pulse becomes more regular and intense as the player approaches higher-level gate infrastructure.\",\n  \"recurring_clue_payoff_hint\": \"When the pulses reach a peak, they reveal a hidden waypoint or a piece of data that is only visible during the 'active' state.\",\n  \"rumor_trail_name\": \"The Ghost Signal Trail\",\n  \"rumor_trail_id\": \"rumor_trail.ghost_signal_trail\",\n  \"rumor_hint_theme\": \"Whispers of a signal that predates known history.\",\n  \"rumor_clue_templates\": [\n    \"A salvage log mentioning 'the hum' in the hull.\",\n    \"A transmission from an Aurelian research ship that went silent suddenly.\"\n  ],\n  \"rumor_discovery_type\": \"hidden_discovery\",\n  \"rumor_rarity\": \"",
